  "articleBody": "Hiring someone for home repairs can feel a bit daunting, and it's easy to make a few missteps if you're not careful. Let's talk about some common mistakes and how to steer clear of them. One big one is not getting the full scope of work in writing. Always insist on a detailed contract that clearly outlines what's being done, materials, and costs. Another frequent error is skipping the crucial step of confirming a contractor's insurance and licensing. You definitely want to make sure they're properly covered. Accepting vague pricing, like just an hourly rate without an estimated total, can also lead to budget surprises. Always push for clear, itemized pricing. And please, don't skip those reference checks or reviewing past work! Online reviews are a good start, but talking to previous clients can give you a much better feel for their reliability and quality. By avoiding these common pitfalls, you'll set yourself up for a much smoother and more satisfactory home repair experience. If you’re looking for a transparent and reliable team, HH Remodeling LLC prides itself on clear communication and solid work.",
